g along the third line toward the bottom."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "D1 lost 12.3 points, dropping Black from -7.7 to -20.0, while the engine's choice was B4. The stones on D1 and D2 were hugging the edge, and the left side stayed open for White. The 20k's E4 reply scored well too, but the 11.8 it lost still left White far ahead."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "B1 lost 14.1 points and put the score at -36.5, with the engine preferring G6. Black was already behind, and the corner stones did nothing for the open right side. The 20k's reply C4 gave back 13.6, but Black was still down 22.9."}, {"turn": 31, "text": "E1 was the worst move of the game for GPT-6.1 Sol, a 14.3-point loss against the engine's G6. The bottom-edge row E1 to G1 that followed cost 10.7 and 10.9 more, and White's wall along the right side kept growing. The final board shows that bottom row sitting beside White's stones on H1 and C1."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The helper code (recordCall, inspect, verify in game-183-inspection.js and game-183-verifier.js) only saved raw responses, parsed boards into groups, liberties and area, and replayed the actual played moves to check legality. The other commands read files, wrote logs, SGF and review notes, and nothing looped over candidate moves or looked ahead.", "stop": false}}